# WOLF AI — Core Engineering

Production trading intelligence. Correctness > polish.

## Before coding

1. Inspect existing services/components/APIs/types first.
2. Reuse → extend → refactor only if needed → create last.
3. Never duplicate pipelines (`MarketDataService2`, parallel feeds, etc.).
4. Change the minimum files; do not casually touch auth, INDstocks, universe, Strategy Lab, charts, DB, or API contracts.

## Market data is source of truth

- Never fabricate LTP, OHLC, volume, OI, option chain, tokens, universes, or FII/DII in production paths.
- If data is missing → explicit unavailable / no-signal — never guess.
- Mock/demo only in isolated modes and must be labeled honestly.

## AI vs math

- Deterministic engines calculate facts (price, RVOL, OI, breakouts, levels).
- AI may **explain** those facts only — never invent prices, indicators, or signals.

## Live systems

- Prefer event-driven updates over polling when a feed exists.
- One normalized market-data pipeline; Radar / Strategy / analytics consume the same state.
- Prefer incremental per-symbol updates over full-universe recalculation.
- Connection states must be honest: CONNECTING / LIVE / RECONNECTING / OFFLINE / MARKET CLOSED.

## Security

- Never expose broker/access/refresh tokens or secrets to browser, URLs, logs, or API errors.
- Keep INDstocks auth on the existing server-side token architecture.

## Change discipline

- Explainable signals only (metrics + triggered/failed conditions).
- Test positive / negative / boundary / missing-data cases for screening logic.
- Verify build/runtime before claiming done.
